.policy "blade-parser-duplicate-condition-expressions" revision 3
.description "Avoid repeating an earlier condition of the same chain in a Blade @elseif; that branch can never run."
.language blade
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.blade.php"

#include "blade/syntax.rr"
//   blade_code(n)   n is in the PHP the template compiles to

// stillat/blade-parser's DuplicateConditionExpressionsValidator: an @elseif whose condition repeats the @if's or an
// earlier @elseif's in the same chain; its branch can never run. Read on the compiled PHP, where the chain is one
// if_statement and its else_if_clauses, each condition the template's own bytes:
//   @if($a) … @elseif($b) … @elseif($a) … @endif      reported at the second @elseif
//   @if($a) … @elseif( $a ) … @endif                  not reported: the text differs (as the validator compares)
.violation duplicate_condition(at: node, c: node) code "DuplicateConditionExpressionsValidator"
    "Change or remove this @elseif; its condition ({c}) already appears earlier in the chain, so the branch never runs."
duplicate_condition(d, c) :- branch(i, d, c), text(c, t), (field(i, "condition", p), child(p, e, 0), text(e, t) ;
    branch(i, d0, e), d0 != d, precedes(d0, d), text(e, t)).
// branch(i, d, c): else_if_clause d of the chain of if_statement i has condition c.
.decl branch(i: node, d: node, c: node)
branch(i, d, c) :- kind(i, "if_statement"), blade_code(i), child(i, d, _), kind(d, "else_if_clause"),
    field(d, "condition", p), child(p, c, 0).
